WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
- Although "The Unholy" is
based on a work of fiction,

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.080
you don't necessarily need
to read the 1983 novel

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.410
to get the most out of the movie.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.880
But there are aspects of the story

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.440
that make reference to real events

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.870
that some have interpreted
as true life miracles.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.440
A few of these instances are called out

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.520
by Bishop James Giles
in a press conference

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.870
as an attempt to explain their
significance to the media.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.480
He quickly summarizes how each of them

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.560
resulted in the nomination
of a holy shrine.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.460
But all of these stories are
at least based on real people.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.550
The first is the case
of Bernadette Soubirous,

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.470
the 14 year old who grew
up in extreme famine

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.070
in the mid 1800s in France.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.430
Bernadette suffered from
intestinal problems and asthma

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.263
since she was little.

00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:34.610
But after experiencing a vision

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.240
of a dazzling white figure as a teen,

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.610
she was supposedly told to
drink this muddy spring water,

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.750
which that day miraculously
turned clear, as the story goes.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.930
The water was said to somehow
be able to cure the sick

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.790
and people assume the spectral visitor

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:47.150
to being the Virgin Mary.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.490
The second case was in 1917 in Portugal

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.160
where three children named
Lucia, Francisco, and Asinta

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.290
reported having encounters

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.090
with apparitions of the Virgin Mary.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.630
Just like the report in
France nearly 60 years before,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.990
they described a woman in white

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.390
exuding a sort of bright
sunlight-like ray.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:03.390
The woman promised the kids
that if they kept coming back,

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.730
she would perform a miracle
on October the 13th,

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:06.980
which involved the sun coming out

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.210
from behind stormy clouds,

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.900
casting multi-colored lights,
and appearing to zoom forward

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.380
and dry the clothes of the
onlookers standing in the rain.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.270
The third and final case
was in 1981 in Bosnia

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.100
where six kids saw a similar woman

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.310
and now many visitors claim
to also be able to see her

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.520
at certain times of day.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.210
The location draws thousands
of pilgrims every year.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.590
Each of these three locations
became holy shrines.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.340
And so, the movie and the book
it's based on, the "Shrine",

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.990
depict the emergence of a
fourth shrine in Massachusetts.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.210
In the story, each of the
three so-called miracles

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.540
were followed up by tragedy,

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.920
which was true in the case of
the three Portuguese children

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.680
who all died in the next one to two years

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.610
during the 1918 flu pandemic.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.280
Ironically, the release of this movie

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.440
would also be hampered
by a major pandemic.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.670
To learn some of the secrets

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.380
of the dark fates behind this event

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.390
once heralded as a modern day miracle,

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.847
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:52.847 --> 00:01:55.514
(ominous music)

00:01:56.897 --> 00:01:59.670
"The Unholy" tells the story
of this small church town

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.660
near Boston being put on the global map

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.800
due to the supposed miracle
that takes place there.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.210
When a deaf and mute girl named Alice

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.640
is gifted with the ability
to hear and speak perfectly.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.330
But one journalist named
Gerry Fenn begins to suspect

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.540
that the entity performing
these supposed miracles

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.370
is anything but a holy one.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.180
Hence, the title of the movie.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.790
Gerry was once a prominent reporter,

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.570
but his desire for fame pushed
him to fabricate stories,

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:23.410
leading to him being shunned
by any respectable publication.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.990
We see he is now working for a site

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.350
called "Bizarre Beantown".

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.250
Beantown is a reference
to the city of Boston

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.820
once known for its baked beans.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.210
But Gerry is sent to the
countryside in Massachusetts

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.400
to investigate a story,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.120
a small town by the name of Banfield.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.770
His story turns out to be a dud.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.380
But when he happens across Alice,

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:41.130
he realizes he's got a much
bigger scoop on his hands

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.800
before eventually discovering
that he may have put himself

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.350
and many others in grave, grave danger.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.170
I've got a few things
you'll want to look out for

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.220
when watching this movie.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.660
So let's get into that.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.618
This video is sponsored by Sony
Pictures Home Entertainment.

00:02:53.618 --> 00:02:56.285
(ominous music)

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.300
When Gerry first arrives in Banfield,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.450
he comes across this doll
known as a Kern Baby,

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.110
which is said to be
planted there by farmers

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.300
as a token of good luck.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.190
However, this particular one is labeled

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.540
with an impossible date,
February 31st, 1945,

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.970
which is said to be part of a practice

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.290
to contain bad spirits.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.550
Little did I know at the time,

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.880
there are actually many
stories of grave markers

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.580
and monuments with this date.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.770
While it can sometimes be used
to denote an unknown date,

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.300
many use it out of superstition.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.090
Essentially, the idea
is that the evil spirit

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.910
will not be released on any anniversary

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.620
because the date listed can never come.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.630
Gerry shows his willingness
to fudge a story for money

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.110
by breaking open the Kern Baby

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.590
and making up a story about
this talisman being broken

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.210
and an unholy evil being
released, thirsty for blood.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.440
In this stance, the story is kind of

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.730
a self-fulfilling prophecy.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:41.340
And this is where we
start to see the signs

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.270
that an evil has indeed been unleashed.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:46.660
But its name is not Virgin
Mary but rather Mary Elnore.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.350
Take the use of color, for example.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.730
We all know from Carrie's mom

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.300
that red is the color of the devil.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.940
And we see that reflected in Alice

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.430
who the satanic entity
speaks to and deceives.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:56.610
When we first lay eyes on her,

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.440
it's the red tail lights of Gerry's truck.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.580
When she gains her hearing back,

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.020
she undergoes an auditory test

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.500
which bathes her in red lights.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.540
The water that Mary Elnore

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.640
emerges from in Gerry's dream is red.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.230
And after she takes her first victim,

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.720
this holy statue is illuminated
in the devil's color.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.920
These are all signs that
what may appear to be holy

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.600
is actually a demonic trick.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.190
Another example of this is the motel

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.690
that Gerry stays in in Banfield.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.240
The sign basks the entire
area in red lights.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:20.610
And in more than one instance,

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.723
Mary Elnore materializes
from that direction.

00:04:23.723 --> 00:04:26.640
(foreboding music)

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.730
(ominous music)

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.440
You'll notice the sign
is always flickering

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.970
and the letter M always flicks

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.480
independently of the other letters.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.540
Could that possibly stand for
Mary, or possibly miracle?

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.120
Either way, it draws my attention.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.430
It makes me think that
something isn't right here.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.610
Alice shows that she's also
able to help other people

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.690
get healed by Mary when
she helps a crippled boy

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:48.790
walk for the first time.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.050
And when she does something like this,

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.490
we see one of these
statutes crying red tears.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.970
We see this happen a few times.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.110
And as a non-Catholic, I was curious about

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.300
what this may have signified.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.270
So I looked it up.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.240
According to this site
called "The Conversation",

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.410
Mary cries not only over
the sins of the world

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.080
but also over the pain she
endured in her early life.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.920
I think the meaning behind
this imagery in the movie

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:08.390
is open to interpretation.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.390
These could be the real
Virgin Mary's tears

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.220
and she's weeping for
everyone who has tricked

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.150
into devoting themselves to a false deity.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.130
Or these could be Mary Elnore's tears

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.810
for the pain that she endured in her life

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.090
which we see in the prologue.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:20.600
I think it's up to you
to be on the lookout

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.570
and make the judgment
as you watch the film.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.000
Another detail I found interesting

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.680
was Alice's music preferences.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.010
Once she gains the ability to hear,

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.680
she takes an interest in country music.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.710
But the song we actually
witnessed her listening to

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:33.100
is "Voices In My Head" by Ashley Tisdale

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.470
which must be connected to the way

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:36.230
that the false spirit
communicates with her

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.237
where she's able to hear
it but nobody else is.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.820
One of the most interesting
character dynamics at play here

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.010
is the relationship
between Gerry and Alice.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.740
Gerry becomes the exclusive
reporter who has access to her.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.030
And in a strange way,

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.730
they both kind of relate to each other.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:50.420
Alice is a girl who was literally able

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:51.900
to use her voice for the first time.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.110
And Gerry has, in essence,
just gotten his voice back,

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.780
or at least his journalistic voice

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.900
after being de platformed

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.490
by the paper that he used to work for.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.130
This makes them built ideal
victims for Mary Elnore

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.070
because they're both
desperate to speak freely.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.550
So despite this movie seeming
to have a bit of a message

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.060
about just being honest
and humble in your work,

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:09.910
you know there's still gonna be

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.260
some true reference Easter eggs.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.180
So here's a few of them
that you can look out for.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.120
During the news and social media montage,

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.490
where a word of Alice's miracle

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:17.700
is spreading around the country,

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:21.350
there's an Instagram post from
an account called joshsg78

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.300
which was likely put there

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.710
by first assistant editor Josh Sgarlata.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.100
Later on, there's a YouTube
live stream of the ceremony

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.060
at the new shrine on Sacrament TV.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.540
Not to be confused with
Sakoda TV from "Death Note".

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.480
There were only three
people active in the chat

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.270
and they include Grace, a
reference to the VFX coordinator

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.550
and Nolan R., the VFX editor.

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.070
I'm not sure who Ron Bingo is,

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.150
but if anyone figures it
out, drop me a comment.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.270
Just taking a quick glance

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:44.540
at some of the ads for this movie,

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.310
I couldn't blame you if
you had the impression

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:49.160
that it was gonna be somewhat
similar to 2018's "The Nun".

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.710
But outside of the generic concept

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.580
of an evil entity posing as a holy one,

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.430
it really couldn't be much more different.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.387
Instead of the expected
haunted house tropes,

00:06:56.387 --> 00:06:58.310
"The Unholy" is more of a character piece

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.260
with the dread that bubbles up
slowly until the big finale.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.456
(fire crackles)

00:07:04.456 --> 00:07:07.860
(crowd screaming)

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.010
You're not gonna see Bloody Mary

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.810
popping up in the mirror for cheap scares.

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.950
And it's kind of refreshing
to see a movie like this

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:16.020
in a modern setting with a touch
of humor where appropriate.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.260
- You have a son?

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.830
- Yeah.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.663
- 16?

00:07:19.663 --> 00:07:20.650
- No, he's 15.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.063
- Do you ever hear of the band Metallica?

00:07:22.063 --> 00:07:24.070
(cow moos)

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.500
- I also mentioned the dream scene

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.610
which offers some surreal
imagery that I liked.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:28.960
But what I was most impressed with

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.180
was the way that the film
handles the antagonist.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.410
Like the characters, we
kind of slowly realized

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.580
that Mary Elnore is not
who she says she is.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.750
But if you look closely,
the clues are there.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.850
When Alice first makes
contact, you can see something

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.110
that looks like a ghostly
figure fade before her,

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.820
which appears again as a glitch
in one of Gerry's videos.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.820
Then when we actually do see the creature

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.390
who fittingly bust out of a statue

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.830
of the actual Virgin Mary,

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:52.160
I won't spoil her appearance
for those who haven't seen it,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.200
but it's like it's a
very own brand of creepy.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.840
And I took a liking to the way it looks,

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.080
the way it moves, and
even the way it sounds.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.420
It was all very unique in
a modern horror landscape

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.020
that already has a lot
of demon characters.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.470
If you haven't seen the
movie yet, you are in luck.

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.500
You can get it now on
digital or on blu-ray.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.610
And if you love horror,

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.310
you're already right where you need to be.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.270
Just go ahead and subscribe to CZsWorld

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:13.610
for new horrors every week.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.700
Ring the death bell for all notifications

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:20.130
and I'll see you in the next
one, assuming we both survive.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:23.800
And if you haven't already,
vaccinate and annihilate.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.050
(upbeat ominous music)

